## 3. Technology Stack (Detailed, by Layer)

### Domain Layer — `StudyHub.Domain`
- **C# / .NET 10**, zero external dependencies (no EF Core, no ASP.NET Core — persistence ignorance).
- Rich domain models: private setters/`init`, private constructors, static factory methods (`Entity.Create(...)`) that enforce business rules at creation time.

### Application Layer — `StudyHub.Application`
- **MediatR** — implements the **CQRS** pattern. Every use case (register, create course, get dashboard...) becomes one `Command` or `Query` object plus one `Handler` class. The API layer never contains business logic — it only sends a request through MediatR.
- **FluentValidation** — validation rules live in dedicated `Validator` classes, separate from the handler logic. Wired into the MediatR pipeline via a `ValidationBehavior`, so **every** Command/Query is validated automatically before its handler ever runs — no manual `if (...) throw` checks scattered across handlers.
- **xUnit + Moq + FluentAssertions** — unit testing stack (see Section 6).
- Repository interfaces (`IUserRepository`, `ICourseRepository`, ...) are **defined here**, not in Infrastructure — this is the Dependency Inversion Principle: Application declares what it needs, Infrastructure provides it.

### Infrastructure Layer — `StudyHub.Infrastructure`
- **EF Core 10** (Code-First) with the **Npgsql** provider for PostgreSQL.
- Implements the repository interfaces declared in Application.
- All entity configuration via **Fluent API only** (`IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>`), one file per entity — no Data Annotations on domain entities.

### API Layer — `StudyHub.API`
- **ASP.NET Core**, thin controllers/endpoints — each one just calls `mediator.Send(command)` and maps the result to an HTTP response.
- **Centralized Global Exception Handling middleware** — no `try/catch` inside controllers for domain exceptions.
- **DTOs** for every request/response — domain entities are never returned directly from an endpoint. (Mapping approach: plain manual mapping via static extension methods for now, e.g. `course.ToDto()` — simplest option, no extra library. Flag it if you'd rather learn AutoMapper/Mapster instead — easy to swap later.)
- **OpenAPI** for API documentation (already scaffolded via `AddOpenApi()`).
- **JWT Bearer authentication** + Refresh Token rotation (UC-01, UC-02).

### Database
- **PostgreSQL 15**, run locally via Docker Compose.
- Referential integrity enforced at the DB level: Foreign Keys + Indexes on every relationship (**implemented** — see Section 7).
- Schema versioned via **EF Core Migrations**.

### DevOps / Tooling
- **Docker Compose** for local PostgreSQL.
- **Git** — trunk-based workflow, `feature/`, `bugfix/`, `chore/` branch prefixes, Conventional Commits (see `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md`).

