## 4. Architectural Decisions (ADRs)

| Component | Decision / Technology | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | C# / .NET 10 | High performance, strong typing, enterprise readiness. |
| Architecture | Clean Architecture (4 Layers) | Separation of concerns, testability, framework independence. |
| Application Pattern | MediatR (CQRS) | Decouples request from handler; one class = one responsibility; easy to add cross-cutting behaviors (validation, logging) without touching every handler. |
| Validation | FluentValidation | Rules separated from handler code, independently testable, integrates cleanly into the MediatR pipeline. |
| Database ORM | EF Core (Code-First) | Rapid development, strong LINQ projection capabilities. |
| Testing | xUnit + Moq | Industry-standard .NET testing stack; Moq fakes repository interfaces so handler tests run in milliseconds with no real database. |
| Security | JWT + Refresh Tokens | Stateless authentication with seamless UX. |
| AI Integration | Gemini AI (Asynchronous API) | Human-in-the-loop: AI suggests tasks, user approves before DB insertion. |

